  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Geared for success&apos; &#x2013; IDP led and RLOs driving education in Uganda &amp; South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective of the project is to enhance equitable and inclusive learning outcomes for refugees, internally displaced people and host communities. This is planned through strengthening the organizational capacity of Community Based Organisations (CBOs) working in the education sector and empowering them for effective delivery of gender -responsive education programming, enhance the ability of women to manage their own time and have agency to play leadership roles in CBOs working in the education sector and  improve social attitudes by host communities, refugees, Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs), and key government stakeholders in support of the role of CBOs. This project is a multi -country project implemented in Uganda and South Sudan in Consortium with War Child Canada. Oxfam will implement the project through local partner in Wau, Malakal and Awerial in South Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
